Ramlah Muhammad Abdallah – Personal Portfolio Website

1. Project Overview

This project is a personal portfolio website developed by Ramlah Muhammad Abdallah, an Information Technology and Software Engineering student aspiring to become a Software Engineer.

The website showcases my personal background, educational journey, interests, projects, and professional aspirations.

It was developed as part of my Web Technologies practical assessment.

2. Project Purpose

The purpose of this project is to:

- Build and demonstrate practical web development skills.
- Create a professional online presence.
- Showcase my academic background and projects.
- Practise HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.
- Develop a responsive and user-friendly website.

3. Technologies Used

- HTML5: Used to structure the website content.
- CSS3: Used for styling, layout, and responsive design.
- JavaScript: Used to provide interactive functionality.
- Git and GitHub: Used for version control and project hosting.
- GitHub Pages: Used to publish the website online.

4. Website Pages and Features

The website consists of five main pages:

Home Page

- Personal introduction.
- Profile photograph.
- Navigation menu.
- Audio introduction.

About Me Page

- Personal background.
- Educational information.
- Skills, interests, and aspirations.

Projects Page

- Displays my projects with screenshots.
- Includes project descriptions.
- Provides links to relevant projects and repositories.

Academic Planner

- Provides an academic task management interface.
- Supports organising academic activities.

Contact Page

- Provides a contact form for visitors.
- Allows visitors to submit their contact information and messages.

